# Milestone 19 — Drop-off Acknowledgment

- **Status:** Not started
- **Objective:** Add the parent drop-off acknowledgment page and `DROPOFF_ACKNOWLEDGED` event, with link-preview safety and first-valid-wins semantics.
- **Dependencies:** 18 (Secure parent session)

## Included work
- Parent-facing drop-off acknowledgment page: minimal JS, mobile-friendly, accessible, no account/email/parent name required.
- Page displays center name, student name, class, time in, and the statement: "I acknowledge that this student was dropped off and checked into the center at the displayed time."
- **"Acknowledge drop-off"** button with explicit confirmation dialog.
- `POST /ack` endpoint: validates token, records `DROPOFF_ACKNOWLEDGED` event, updates session status/timestamp/masked phone ref.
- `GET` requests never complete actions; link-preview bots and known crawler user-agents receive a no-op safe page.
- First valid acknowledgment wins; the other parent's link shows "already acknowledged."
- Expired/completed links show a clear explanation.
- CSRF and replay protection.
- SMS link inclusion in the check-in SMS template (local link in local-only mode).
- Unit and integration tests.

## Explicitly excluded work
- No pickup acknowledgment page (deferred to M20).
- No remote relay (deferred to M30).
- No real SMS sending (deferred to M29); dev outbox includes the link.

## Expected files or directories
- `apps/local-server/src/parent/dropoff-page.ts`
- `apps/local-server/src/routes/ack.ts`
- `apps/local-server/src/parent/link-preview.ts`
- `apps/local-server/src/__tests__/dropoff-ack.test.ts`
- `apps/local-server/src/__tests__/link-preview.test.ts`

## Acceptance criteria
- The drop-off page loads quickly with minimal JS and is mobile-friendly.
- Pressing "Acknowledge drop-off" with confirmation records the event.
- Merely opening the link does not count as acknowledgment.
- GET never completes the action.
- Link-preview bots receive a no-op page.
- First valid acknowledgment wins; the second link shows "already acknowledged."
- Expired/completed links show a clear explanation.
- The drop-off acknowledgment time appears separately from Student time in.
- `npm run typecheck` and `npm run test` pass.

## Required automated tests
- Drop-off acknowledgment success.
- Duplicate drop-off acknowledgment rejected (first wins).
- Expired token rejected.
- Reused token rejected.
- Revoked token rejected.
- Link-preview bot no-op.
- GET does not complete action.

## Manual verification steps
1. Check in a student and open the drop-off link from the dev outbox SMS.
2. Press "Acknowledge drop-off" and confirm.
3. Open the second parent's link and confirm it shows "already acknowledged."

